c3-guide-mcp contains material from other projects:

- data/corpus.dat is a snapshot generated from the C3 project (https://github.com/c3lang/c3c and
  https://c3-lang.org): the language manual, the release notes, and the documentation and signatures
  of the standard library. The C3 project licenses everything outside the compiler source (src/) under
  the MIT license; this includes the standard library and its documentation. The snapshot is
  Copyright (c) the C3 contributors.
- deps/mcp.c3l (a git submodule, pinned to a commit) is the MCP SDK by Koni Marti, MIT.

- vendor/tree-sitter (a git submodule, pinned to v0.27.1, https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter), MIT,
  Copyright (c) 2018 Max Brunsfeld. vendor/tree-sitter-c3 (a git submodule, pinned to v0.13.0,
  https://github.com/c3lang/tree-sitter-c3), MIT, Copyright (c) 2024 Christian Buttner. Only the runtime
  and the generated parser are compiled into the binary; each submodule keeps its own LICENSE.

The compiler c3c itself (LGPL 3.0) is not included or linked: c3_check starts it as a separate process
from the user's installation.
